<description>
Fill the black holes by continuing the smallest repeating non-black wallpaper pattern.

Input structure:
- The grid is a rectangular wallpaper pattern with some cells replaced by black.
- Every phase of the true repeating tile is visible at least once in a non-black cell.
- The smallest fully observed tile consistent with the non-black cells is unique.

Rule:
- Ignore black pixels while inferring the repeating tile.
- Find the unique minimal-area tile whose row/column phases agree with all non-black cells.
- Replace every grid cell by the color at its corresponding tile phase.

Key insight:
- Black is missing data, not part of the wallpaper; the observed colored cells determine the latent periodic tile.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "non-black cells of a periodic wallpaper with black holes",
  "transform": "infer the unique minimal repeating tile from row/column phases of the non-black cells, then replace every black pixel with the tile color at the same phase"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 25x25 (constant across all examples)
  tile:
    size: 4-9 rows x 2-9 cols; area 8-81
    structure: row 0 and col 0 are all-blue(1) grid lines; may have additional interior all-blue rows/cols at regular intervals
    inner_region: cells excluding all-blue rows/cols; LR and UD symmetric [observed]
    colors: 3-4 distinct non-black colors including blue(1); 2-3 non-blue colors
    no_black: tile never contains black
    uniqueness: must be the unique minimal-area tile consistent with non-black cells
  wallpaper: output is the tile repeated (tiled) to fill the 25x25 grid
  black_holes:
    count: 3-4 contiguous 4-connected blobs of black(0) replacing wallpaper cells
    total_fraction: 8-13% of grid cells
    per_blob_size: 4-55 cells; bbox 2x2 to 11x9
    position: never touch grid border (min 1-cell margin from all edges)
    fill_ratio: 0.56-1.00 of bounding box (rectangles and irregular shapes both occur)
    coverage: after removing black blobs, every tile phase (r%tile_h, c%tile_w) must still be observed at least once among remaining non-black cells
  input: wallpaper with black holes (some cells replaced by black)
  output: complete wallpaper with all black holes filled in

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose tile_h in [4..9], tile_w in [2..9]. Pick 2-3 non-blue colors. Fill tile[0,:]=1, tile[:,0]=1. Optionally add interior all-blue grid-line rows/cols at regular spacing. Fill inner region with chosen colors, enforcing LR+UD symmetry.
    2. Tile the 25x25 grid by repeating the tile to get the output.
    3. Place 3-4 black blobs. For each, pick a random connected region (rectangle or irregular shape) of 4-55 cells, ensuring no border touching and blobs don't merge.
    4. Verify coverage constraint -- every tile phase (r%th, c%tw) has at least one non-black cell remaining. If not, shrink the largest blob or retry placement.
    5. Input = output with black-blob cells set to 0.
